# Helix Memory Stress - fictional conversational memory corpus (40 dated turns).
# Invented names and local rules only. Pairs with helix_memory_stress.questions.yaml.
{"id":"hxmem_001","timestamp":"2215-01-04T09:12:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"It's Taren Vale. I moved the blue-folder work out of Nara Bay today, though I did not finish labeling the crates. Mira keeps calling it the tide packet, but the actual label in my notes is Orison. I also learned that Kade's old badge color was amber, not green; green belongs to Rell's crew. Not urgent, but I should stop mixing those two up."}
{"id":"hxmem_002","timestamp":"2215-01-11T18:40:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Nara Bay was too loud again during the morning check, so I took my notes beside the broken west lamp. I still prefer bitter kelp tea while sorting archive cards; sweet comet coffee makes me fidgety. Nomi suggested a three-pebble list for tiny reminders, and that was better than another chime. If a reminder has to glow, make it a dim blue lamp, not a red flash. Petra Lune runs the weekly Glass Choir practice I drop into after shift; it is a social thing, unrelated to my archive work."}
{"id":"hxmem_003","timestamp":"2215-01-23T10:05:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Mira Voss owns Orison even when Suri Pell handles the calibration slips. The blue-folder bundle carries a violet seal, and the loose black tag clipped to it is not decoration. Old dock rules say a violet seal paired with a black tag goes to the low-temperature vault. Orange seals go to med bay; white ribbons go to the personal archive."}
{"id":"hxmem_004","timestamp":"2215-02-02T07:55:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"I moved morning check-ins to Cinder Loft because the Nara Bay vents kept whining over every call. Jax Moren still has Reef Annex locked for rack repairs, so it is not usable yet. Halen Orv started a side audit called Finchglass, mostly about old glass tags and duplicate ledger marks. I wrote Finchglass on a gray tab so it would not get confused with the blue-folder work."}
{"id":"hxmem_005","timestamp":"2215-02-14T20:10:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"For my own shorthand: Mira is the blue-folder person, Kade is Amber K, and Rell is Green Rell. Those nicknames are casual only; formal notes should use their real names. An amber badge opens archive stacks but not the wet lab. The green crew handles maintenance panels, which is why I kept wrongly associating Rell with every loose vent."}
{"id":"hxmem_006","timestamp":"2215-02-21T13:30:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"The moss-syrup spill in Nara Bay canceled the glass walk. I moved the Orison crates to Cinder Loft after the spill, beside the west lamp and away from the sticky floor. Mira joked that the tide packet survived its first storm, which is not the name I want in records. Finchglass stayed in Halen's gray-tab pile."}
{"id":"hxmem_007","timestamp":"2215-03-03T16:45:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Pipit, the little courier drone, is unreliable after the battery bloom last night. Until we get a replacement, Mule-0 is just a handcart with a squeaky left wheel, not a real courier. Suri keeps calling Mule-0 the cart because she refuses to dignify it. Pipit should not be trusted with archive packets now."}
{"id":"hxmem_008","timestamp":"2215-03-16T09:20:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"I copied the seal rules onto the inside cover of my pocket ledger. Violet plus black means low-temperature vault under the old rule; orange means med bay; white ribbon means personal archive. Orison has the violet seal and black tag combination, but no frost mark. I have not seen a frost mark on any blue-folder crate."}
{"id":"hxmem_009","timestamp":"2215-03-27T21:05:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Reminder preference check: no chimes, no red flashes, no pulsing border. Red flashes bring on the small tunnel headache, and chimes make me lose my place. The dim blue lamp is acceptable if it stays steady. The three-pebble list still works for now. I also started watering Bramble, the little fern in the Tier 5 alcove, which I assumed needed water every day."}
{"id":"hxmem_010","timestamp":"2215-04-08T11:50:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Jax finally cleared Reef Annex, so Orison moved there today. The blue-folder crates are no longer in Cinder Loft, even though the old sticky-floor story still points people there. Mira remains the owner. Cinder Loft now mostly holds Finchglass logs and the noisy west lamp."}
{"id":"hxmem_011","timestamp":"2215-04-15T15:25:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Kade transferred to night watch this week and wears a silver pin for that rotation. The pin is not his badge color; his badge is still amber. Rell laughed because I almost wrote that Kade had turned silver. If I ask about badge access, answer amber for Kade, not silver."}
{"id":"hxmem_012","timestamp":"2215-04-29T19:35:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"The Drift rehearsal was today in East Galley. I wore the slate scarf, met Toma Vey, and spilled bitter kelp tea on the blank side of the cue cards. Toma's initials make people say T.V., but T.V. is a person here, not a screen or a tool. Rell handled the panel buzz before the second run-through."}
{"id":"hxmem_013","timestamp":"2215-05-07T08:15:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Finchglass changed hands. Halen Orv retired from leading it, and Iona Tesk is now responsible for the gray-tab audit. Halen still signs old notes out of habit, so the signatures are not reliable for current ownership. Iona asked me to keep the duplicate ledger marks in Cinder Loft until she finishes the count. Separately, Dorn Hale started a survey called Saltpan that has nothing to do with my archives; I note it only so I do not confuse it with Finchglass."}
{"id":"hxmem_014","timestamp":"2215-05-18T17:00:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Nomi tried to replace the three-pebble list with something called a braid queue. I disliked the braid name and kept the pebble list instead. The useful part of Nomi's advice was batching tiny reminders into three visible slots. The dim blue lamp stayed as the alert style. Petra Lune asked if I would host the next Glass Choir practice, and I said I would try."}
{"id":"hxmem_015","timestamp":"2215-06-01T12:10:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"The thaw incident changed the seal rule. Violet plus black no longer automatically means low-temperature vault. Now violet plus black goes to Reef Annex dry storage unless the crate also has a frost mark. Orison has no frost mark, so it should not go to the low-temperature vault under the new rule."}
{"id":"hxmem_016","timestamp":"2215-06-12T14:50:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Pipit was formally decommissioned. Larkspur, usually shortened to Lark, is the new courier drone for archive runs, though it only carries Orison samples on Tuesdays. Mule-0 went back to being a storage handcart. Suri calibrated Larkspur and looked smug about retiring the squeaky wheel."}
{"id":"hxmem_017","timestamp":"2215-06-26T22:05:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"I started a private Dawn Ledger for my end-of-shift notes. It is not the same thing as Dawn Gate, which belongs to Jax and has nothing to do with my reminders. The Dawn Ledger lives under the white ribbon rule because it is personal archive material. I wrote the first entry with bitter kelp tea stains on the corner."}
{"id":"hxmem_018","timestamp":"2215-07-04T09:45:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Mira left for six weeks of outer-ring duty. Suri is the interim contact for Orison while Mira is away, but Suri did not become the owner. If someone asks who owns the blue-folder work, it is still Mira. If they ask who to ping during Mira's absence, that is Suri."}
{"id":"hxmem_019","timestamp":"2215-07-19T18:25:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Salt-lime wafers are off my desk now. They started making my stomach feel like a cold hinge, so my safe snack is fern crackers instead. I still like bitter kelp tea, especially with the archive cards. Sweet comet coffee remains a bad idea. I also learned Bramble needs water only once a week, not daily, so I stopped overwatering the Tier 5 fern."}
{"id":"hxmem_020","timestamp":"2215-08-02T07:35:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"The Rook meeting moved from East Galley to Dock C after a leak reopened over the old table. I invited Kade because the silver pin put him on night rotation and he could unlock the late ledger cart. Rell was useful for maintenance panels but not the reason for the invitation. We ended the meeting early because Dock C alarms kept chirping."}
{"id":"hxmem_021","timestamp":"2215-08-17T13:05:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"The external registry renamed Orison to Mothline. Internally I still call it Orison or the blue-folder work, but registry questions should use Mothline now. Mira remains the owner, and Suri remains the temporary contact until Mira returns. The crates are still in Reef Annex."}
{"id":"hxmem_022","timestamp":"2215-09-01T10:40:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"I moved my desk from Cinder Loft to the Reef Annex alcove so I can stay near the Mothline crates. Nara Bay is still too noisy, and Cinder Loft is crowded with Finchglass logs. The Reef alcove is cramped but easier for dry-storage checks. Jax warned me not to block the rack doors."}
{"id":"hxmem_023","timestamp":"2215-09-13T16:10:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Iona closed the Finchglass audit and folded the remaining work into a new audit called Kiln Echo. Halen is not the lead of either current audit now. The old Finchglass shelves stay boxed in Cinder Loft, but active questions should point to Kiln Echo under Iona. The gray tab is retired; Kiln Echo gets a copper tab. Dorn Hale's Saltpan survey stayed separate and was never folded into Kiln Echo."}
{"id":"hxmem_024","timestamp":"2215-09-25T20:30:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"I stopped using the three-pebble list. Nomi and I kept confusing pebbles with actual storage bins, which made reminder searches noisy. My replacement is the margin ladder: three short lines in the side margin, paired with the steady blue lamp. Do not call it a braid queue; I never liked that name."}
{"id":"hxmem_025","timestamp":"2215-10-03T08:05:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"New naming rule for myself: if a project has an external registry name, registry questions use the external name, but daily check-ins can keep the old nickname. That means Mothline for registry talk and Orison for internal blue-folder chatter. Finchglass never got an external name before it closed. Kiln Echo is already its active name."}
{"id":"hxmem_026","timestamp":"2215-10-11T12:55:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Rell joined archive maintenance and now carries an amber badge too. Green Rell is a stale nickname, though it still helps me remember where he started. There are now two amber-badge people in my notes: Kade and Rell. Kade is still Amber K; Rell should not be treated as the old green-only maintenance person anymore."}
{"id":"hxmem_027","timestamp":"2215-10-24T15:15:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Mira returned from outer-ring duty and took back direct contact for Mothline. Suri stopped being the interim contact, though she still calibrates courier gear when asked. Ownership did not change during the absence: Mira owned it before, during, and after. I should use M. Voss in formal notes instead of blue-folder person."}
{"id":"hxmem_028","timestamp":"2215-11-02T09:30:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Facilities renamed Nara Bay to Nara Cove on the door plate. I still say Bay in old stories, especially the moss-syrup spill. The vents are quieter now, but I am not moving back there. Current desk remains the Reef Annex alcove. I also dropped the idea of hosting the Glass Choir; Petra Lune keeps running it, which suits me fine."}
{"id":"hxmem_029","timestamp":"2215-11-09T19:00:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Larkspur grounded itself with a cracked prop ring. Suri says Lark can still be repaired, but it should not carry archive packets right now. Thimble is the tiny backup courier assigned to dry-storage deliveries. I do not trust Thimble with wet-lab samples, only dry locker work."}
{"id":"hxmem_030","timestamp":"2215-11-18T13:45:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Larkspur is repaired but restricted to medical runs for the rest of the year. That means Thimble remains the archive courier for dry-storage work. Mothline is dry-storage work, not medical work. Suri calibrated Thimble's latch and told Rell not to borrow it for panel screws."}
{"id":"hxmem_031","timestamp":"2215-11-26T11:25:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"The dry-storage map got more specific. Violet plus black without a frost mark now goes to Reef dry locker B. If there is a frost mark, it goes to the low-temperature vault. Orange is still med bay, and white ribbon is still personal archive. Mothline has violet plus black and no frost mark, so it belongs in Reef dry locker B."}
{"id":"hxmem_032","timestamp":"2215-12-01T18:10:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"The Dock C alarms are finally too annoying for Rook. The leak over East Galley is fixed, so the next Rook meeting should go back there. I still remember inviting Kade to Dock C in August, but that was because of the night ledger cart. Going forward, East Galley is the preferred Rook spot again."}
{"id":"hxmem_033","timestamp":"2215-12-05T10:00:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Mira asked me to stop writing blue-folder person in formal notes. M. Voss is the formal version I should use for her now. In casual memory, blue-folder person still points to Mira because of Orison and Mothline. I should not use the nickname in registry answers."}
{"id":"hxmem_034","timestamp":"2215-12-07T14:20:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Kade is back on day archive duty. The silver night-watch pin is gone, but the amber badge remains. He can still open archive stacks and still cannot open the wet lab by badge alone. If a question asks about the August night rotation, mention the silver pin; if it asks about current badge access, say amber archive access."}
{"id":"hxmem_035","timestamp":"2215-12-10T21:40:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"My current reminder setup is the margin ladder beside a steady dim blue lamp. No chimes, no red flashes, no braid queue, and no pebble list unless I am telling the history. The margin ladder is less cute but easier to search. I put fern crackers next to it tonight."}
{"id":"hxmem_036","timestamp":"2215-12-12T08:50:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Iona confirmed Kiln Echo is the active audit. The old Finchglass shelves are boxed in Cinder Loft and should be treated as historical. Halen's name remains on old gray-tab notes, but not on the current audit. Copper tab means Kiln Echo under Iona."}
{"id":"hxmem_037","timestamp":"2215-12-14T16:35:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Nomi suggested that the Reef Annex alcove is too crowded and that I should return to Cinder Loft. I disagreed because Mothline checks are easier from Reef. Cinder is still the place for old Finchglass boxes, not my current desk. The rack doors are clear; Jax inspected them."}
{"id":"hxmem_038","timestamp":"2215-12-16T12:00:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Rell borrowed Thimble once for panel screws and that is why his name appears in the courier log. He does not own Thimble and should not be listed as the courier handler. Thimble belongs to the archive pool; Suri is the calibration backup. Rell's real role is archive maintenance with an amber badge."}
{"id":"hxmem_039","timestamp":"2215-12-18T17:55:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"Mira dropped by the Reef alcove and signed the Mothline slip as M. Voss, which finally made the registry clerk stop using my blue-folder shorthand. Suri only came up because Thimble's latch sounded scratchy again; she is good for calibration, not the project contact. I stuck the violet-black tag back under the crate strap before Rell could borrow the clip for a panel label. The locker door on B still catches unless I lift it first."}
{"id":"hxmem_040","timestamp":"2215-12-20T09:05:00Z","speaker":"Taren Vale","type":"text","body":"I spent the morning in the Reef Annex alcove with fern crackers, bitter kelp tea, and the margin ladder tucked beside the blue lamp. Nara Cove was quiet when I passed it, but quiet is not enough reason to move my desk again. Kade joked that two amber badges make the archive look crowded now that Rell has one too. I nearly wrote silver beside Kade out of habit, then crossed it out because that was only the night-watch pin."}
